  "worldattribute-terraindiffusionAltitudeCooling": "Altitude cooling",
  "worldattribute-terraindiffusionAltitudeCooling-desc": "How fast it gets colder going up. 100% is the model's own climate; every 100% above that takes another 6.5 C off per kilometre of height, at the ground and in the air alike, so mountains get colder with lower treelines and snowlines. Sea level is unchanged.",
  "worldattribute-terraindiffusionAltitudeCooling-unit": "{0}%",
  "worldattribute-terraindiffusionForestDensity": "Forest density",
  "worldattribute-terraindiffusionForestDensity-desc": "Scales the forest cover the model's climate implies. Trees on the ground go roughly as the square of this: 140% is about twice the trees.",
  "worldattribute-terraindiffusionForestDensity-unit": "{0}%",
  "worldattribute-terraindiffusionShrubDensity": "Shrub density",
  "worldattribute-terraindiffusionShrubDensity-desc": "Scales shrub cover the same way, with the same squaring.",
  "worldattribute-terraindiffusionShrubDensity-unit": "{0}%",
  "worldattribute-terraindiffusionWinterAmplification": "Winter severity",
  "worldattribute-terraindiffusionWinterAmplification-desc": "How much deeper winters get away from the equator: below the annual mean, temperatures swing further by this share at the poles, half of it halfway there. 80% matches vanilla's coldest months. Summers are unchanged; can be changed at any time.",
  "worldattribute-terraindiffusionBandedRainfallBias": "Banded rainfall correction",
  "worldattribute-terraindiffusionBandedRainfallBias-desc": "Asks the model for a third less rain along the latitude bands, a correction measured on the original latitude profile. Off for new worlds.",
  "worldattribute-terraindiffusionRiverValleyDepth": "River valley depth",
  "worldattribute-terraindiffusionRiverValleyDepth-desc": "How far the land is lowered where the Rivers mod runs a river, so the model shapes a valley to carry it. Needs that mod. High values sink river corridors below sea level and turn them into inlets.",
  "worldattribute-terraindiffusionRiverValleyDepth-unit": "{0}%",
  "worldattribute-terraindiffusionWaterFill": "Lakes and rivers",
  "worldattribute-terraindiffusionWaterFill-desc": "Fills closed basins above sea level with fresh water up to where they spill, and cuts rivers into the land. Off leaves the land dry.",
  "worldattribute-terraindiffusionWetlandDepth": "Wetland depth",
  "worldattribute-terraindiffusionWetlandDepth-desc": "Lakes stand this many blocks below where they would spill over. The shallow ground they leave becomes wetland at the waterline: marsh with scattered pools and reeds, which rivers run through. 0 fills every lake to the brim.",
  "worldattribute-terraindiffusionWetlandDepth-unit": "{0} blocks",
  "worldattribute-terraindiffusionRiverMode": "Rivers",
  "worldattribute-terraindiffusionRiverMode-desc": "Which rivers are cut into the land: trunk only the main rivers, river and creek progressively smaller ones. Off leaves only lakes.",
  "worldconfig-terraindiffusionRiverMode-off": "off",
  "worldconfig-terraindiffusionRiverMode-creek": "creek",
  "worldconfig-terraindiffusionRiverMode-river": "river",
  "worldconfig-terraindiffusionRiverMode-trunk": "trunk",
  "worldattribute-terraindiffusionRiverTrim": "River trim",
  "worldattribute-terraindiffusionRiverTrim-desc": "Cuts a river only where it carries at least this share of the biggest river the world tells apart, trimming the small tributaries. Applies on top of Rivers; 0 keeps every river that mode allows.",
  "worldattribute-terraindiffusionRiverTrim-unit": "{0}%",
  "worldattribute-terraindiffusionRiverWidth": "River width",
  "worldattribute-terraindiffusionRiverWidth-desc": "Multiplies the width and depth of every river. x1 is true to scale, where almost every river is one block wide; larger values make rivers easier to see and to sail.",
  "worldattribute-terraindiffusionRiverWidth-unit": "x{0}",
