  "worldattribute-terraindiffusionInferenceDevice": "Inference device",
  "worldattribute-terraindiffusionInferenceDevice-desc": "Which execution provider runs the model. OpenVINO is primarily for Linux servers. TensorRT RTX needs a GeForce RTX 30xx or newer on Windows or Linux and is roughly 1.5x faster than CUDA. CUDA is another option for Nvidia GPUs. ROCm runs AMD GPUs on Linux and needs ROCm 7 with MIGraphX installed; the first run compiles each model for the GPU, which can take several minutes. \"auto\" picks CoreML on macOS, DirectML on Windows, CUDA on Linux with an NVIDIA GPU and the CUDA toolkit installed, and the CPU everywhere else. Changing provider can alter newly generated terrain slightly. Takes effect the next time the world is loaded.",
  "worldconfig-terraindiffusionInferenceDevice-auto": "Auto (recommended)",
  "worldconfig-terraindiffusionInferenceDevice-cpu": "CPU only",
  "worldconfig-terraindiffusionInferenceDevice-openvino": "OpenVINO (Linux CPU)",
  "worldconfig-terraindiffusionInferenceDevice-cuda": "CUDA (NVIDIA)",
  "worldconfig-terraindiffusionInferenceDevice-tensorrt-rtx": "TensorRT RTX (NVIDIA RTX 30xx+)",
  "worldconfig-terraindiffusionInferenceDevice-rocm": "ROCm (AMD, Linux)",
  "worldconfig-terraindiffusionInferenceDevice-directml": "DirectML (Windows)",
  "worldconfig-terraindiffusionInferenceDevice-coreml": "CoreML (macOS)",
  "worldattribute-terraindiffusionDecoderPrecision": "Decoder precision",
  "worldattribute-terraindiffusionDecoderPrecision-desc": "FP32 is the default. FP16 provides better performance, but kinda sucks atm. INT8 is a smaller decoder for the CPU and OpenVINO. Neither is ever selected automatically because both can alter newly generated terrain slightly. FP16 needs a GPU provider, a world set to it on a machine without one does not load.",
  "worldconfig-terraindiffusionDecoderPrecision-fp32": "FP32",
  "worldconfig-terraindiffusionDecoderPrecision-fp16": "FP16",
  "worldconfig-terraindiffusionDecoderPrecision-int8": "INT8",
  "worldattribute-terraindiffusionBasePrecision": "Base model precision",
  "worldattribute-terraindiffusionBasePrecision-desc": "The base model is most of the work in a tile. FP16 with TensorRT-RTX is the fastest, but the default is FP32 until the FP16 model can be improved. FP16 needs a GPU provider, a world set to it on a machine without one does not load.",
  "worldconfig-terraindiffusionBasePrecision-fp32": "FP32",
  "worldconfig-terraindiffusionBasePrecision-fp16": "FP16",
  "worldattribute-terraindiffusionGpuUtilizationPercent": "GPU utilisation limit",
  "worldattribute-terraindiffusionGpuUtilizationPercent-unit": "{0}%",
  "worldattribute-terraindiffusionGpuUtilizationPercent-desc": "Share of the time world generation may keep the inference device busy. Tweaking this may help with stuttering, but can also cause stuttering. Can be changed with /tdiff gpulimit in game.",
  "worldattribute-terraindiffusionCpuThreads": "CPU threads",
  "worldattribute-terraindiffusionCpuThreads-desc": "How many CPU threads run the model when it runs on the CPU (CPU only, OpenVINO, or a GPU that could not start). Auto is one per physical core, or every thread for OpenVINO. Fewer leaves more for the game. Does not change the terrain. Takes effect the next time the world is loaded.",
  "worldattribute-terraindiffusionCpuThreads-unit": "{0}",
